MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2025-04-09T11:28:54Z","updated_at":"2025-04-11T10:28:03Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in: v4.4.stable.arch_linux, v4.5.dev.custom_build [8bd9cdeea]\nThis also appeared in v4.3.stable.arch_linux at least since January 15. 2025\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.dev (8bd9cdeea) - Arch Linux #1 ZEN SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Sun, 23 Mar 2025 17:17:17 +0000 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Single-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated AMD Radeon Graphics (RADV RENOIR) - AMD Ryzen 5 7530U with Radeon Graphics (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nEnabling transparent Viewport removes Fog and Volumetric fog. This also happens when setting transparent background in a subviewport. \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nThere is almost no setup.\n1) Create a scene with an environment and enable volumetric fog.\n2) Enable Transparent Viewport\n3) The fog is gone.\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nThe effect is more visible when adding a fogvolume to a scene and setting volumetric fog densitiy to 0 in the environment. \nWhen turning of the transparency, the fog is correctly visible. Enabling the transparency results in the fog being hidden.\nI tested this on Windows as well and it also happens there.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105186/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0